From 0f187774349dd523e954f974393d5cfe4f6c110b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KenshiCoop player report <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:40:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] coop: re-keyed bodies stop flickering, and a placed door
 opens on both screens

Two identity-translation gaps found in a two-PC field session (v0.51,
KENSHICOOP_CELL_AUTH=0 on both clients, both players in one town).

RE-KEYED BODIES WERE CULLED BY THE WIDE CENSUS PASS. When a fight starts the
engine separateIntoMyOwnSquad's a town NPC into a fresh local container, so
the join's copy gets a new local hand. The drive already logs the translation
([rekey] wire=... local=...), but enforceHostAuthority's wide pass looked the
LOCAL hand up in a census keyed by the host's hand, missed, and culled the
body; the next drive sample restored it (proxy/driven exemption) and the cycle
repeated. In 17 minutes the join logged 1303 wide culls and 1273 restores -
1275 of the culls (98%) on 9 re-keyed bodies, one 'Shek Retainer' 702 times.
Players see the same townspeople blink in and out.

The drive now records the reverse map (wireOfLocal_, local -> wire) whenever a
driven body's local hand diverges from its wire key. It is not pruned with
drivenSeen_/canonicalOf_ (30 s), because the wide pass needs it exactly after
the stream has moved on; hands are serial-checked so a stale entry can only
match the body it was stamped for, and it is cleared in resetSession. The wide
pass treats a body as existing when its translated wire key is in the census
or in this tick's streamed set.

A PLACED BUILDING THAT IS ITSELF A DOOR NEVER SYNCED ITS STATE. Forgotten
Buildings makes 'Storm House Door E' (4029-TwoStorey.mod) placeable on its
own. It has no parent building, so the protocol-28 partition never claims it
and publishDoors streams it on protocol 26 under the placer's runtime hand -
which names nothing on the peer, whose copy is the proxy minted from the
PLACE (mint OK, dy=0.0). applyDoors' readDoorByHand failed and the row was
dropped as "runtime door - accepted edge": the placer logged
'[door] SEND ... open=1' and the join logged no [door] line at all, so the
door stayed shut on one screen.

publishDoors now sends a minted proxy door under the placer's wire key
(mintByLocal_), and applyDoors resolves an inbound placer key through
peerBuilds_ to the local proxy (also seeding that local row's baseline as the
echo guard). Doors that come from the save, and doors that are children of
placed buildings (protocol 28), are unaffected. No wire change; no log string
changed.

Not built or run against the harness: checked with clang -fsyntax-only
(C++03, stubbed windows.h, real enet headers) on the four touched TUs only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nx3WGAiNWtET5BLWsyajcy
